cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it as below, and cite the original
  paper it reproduces (see references). This is an independent, third-party
  reproduction and is NOT the paper's own code -- see README_REPRODUCTION.md
  and docs/source_inventory.md for exactly what is and is not verified against
  the original.
title: >-
  A Reproduction of "Pushing the Limits of Inverse Lithography with
  Generative Reinforcement Learning"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/tangtangtang19871987-wq/VibeCodeProj_A01
keywords:
  - inverse lithography
  - computational lithography
  - ILT
  - OPC
  - optical proximity correction
  - reinforcement learning
  - generative adversarial networks
  - semiconductor manufacturing
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      Pushing the Limits of Inverse Lithography with Generative
      Reinforcement Learning
    authors:
      - family-names: Yang
        given-names: Haoyu
      - family-names: Ren
        given-names: Haoxing
    year: 2026
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2602.19027v1"
        description: arXiv preprint identifier
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.19027
    notes: >-
      The paper this repository reproduces. 63rd Design Automation Conference
      (DAC'26). Authors are affiliated with NVIDIA Corp.
  - type: generic
    title: ICCAD-2013 CAD contest in mask optimization and benchmark suite
    authors:
      - family-names: Banerjee
        given-names: Shayak
      - family-names: Li
        given-names: Zhuo
      - family-names: Nassif
        given-names: Sani R.
    year: 2013
    notes: >-
      Source of the public ICCAD13 benchmark layouts and the L2/PV-Band/EPE
      scoring protocol this repository reproduces bit-exactly. See
      docs/source_inventory.md S2.1.
  - type: software
    title: OpenILT
    repository-code: https://github.com/OpenOPC/OpenILT
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Public source of the 24-term SOCS optical kernels and the reference
      ICCAD13 scoring implementation this repository's physics stack is
      checksummed and validated against. Not the target paper's own code.
      See docs/source_inventory.md S2.2-S2.5 and docs/findings.md F-ADJ-01
      for a correction found in its reference adjoint implementation.
